{"id":"20260826T003052.974560699Z-4768a0c4","time":"2026-08-26T00:30:52.974560699Z","session_id":"session-20260826T002520.251912383Z","task_id":"task-1787703920252134578","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  The abandoned-worktree check treats a candidate directory containing only this tool's own artefacts as if it held the user's work, so a repository is reported as holding abandoned work when it holds none, and nothing offers to clean it up.\n\nA candidate whose contents are entirely artefacts this tool created must not be described as holding work, and must be removable automatically. A candidate holding anything the user could have written must still be preserved and reported for a person to decide. Dot-directories beside a candidate are this tool's own and are not candidates.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] The current check classifies every non-empty, non-live directory beneath the sibling worktree root as an abandoned candidate holding files; only empty directories receive an automatic repair. (internal/setup/checks.go:checkAbandonedWorktrees) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The current repair rechecks emptiness before removing a directory, but cannot remove a directory containing recognised tool artefacts. (internal/setup/checks.go:removeAll) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Candidate worktrees use a `.git` entry as their repository-confirmed worktree marker. (internal/gitx/git.go:CreateWorktree) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The workflow installs its `.guard` directory beside the candidate rather than inside it. (internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.runCandidate) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Inspection returns repairs without executing them, and the CLI invokes those repairs only after `--apply` is selected. (internal/setup/inspect.go:InspectRepository, internal/setup/setup.go:Apply, cmd/sensei-code/setup.go:runSetup) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Repository intent requires preserving candidates that may contain unreviewed work and keeping tool artefacts out of candidate changes. (docs/intent/sensei_code.candidates_are_isolated.yaml) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei records as critical that candidate disposition be decided and evidence outlive removal. (invariant:sensei_code.candidate.disposition_is_decided_and_evidence_outlives_removal) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei records as critical that reviewers see every changed file, including worker-created files. (invariant:sensei_code.candidate.reviewer_sees_every_changed_file) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei's accepted setup decision keeps inspection read-only and repair behavior exclusive to the existing apply flow. (decision:decision.sensei_code.add_a_read_only_tui_readiness_report_command_keep_all_repair) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Scoped preflight examined both planned files, classified the change as local and low risk, and found no directly anchored governing rule; confidence remains low. (internal/setup/checks.go and internal/setup/setup_test.go) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
